DP  - 2010 Sep
TI  - TB or not TB: update from the ERS Respiratory Infection Assembly 10.
PG  - 665-70
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00054410 [doi]
AB  - Lower respiratory tract infections and tuberculosis represent some of the top 
      health priorities in Europe. In the present report, the most recent advances in 
      the field of disease control, clinical research and basic science of lower 
      respiratory tract infections and tuberculosis are presented through analysis of 
      some of the best abstracts presented at the 19th European Respiratory Society 
      Congress in Vienna (Austria). Pathogenesis, diagnosis, treatment, prognostic 
      factors and novel diagnostic techniques relevant for bacterial and viral 
      infections, as well as new tools for the diagnosis of latent and active 
      tuberculosis in different sub-groups of patients, are discussed. The growing 
      epidemiological threat represented by multidrug-resistant and extensively 
      drug-resistant tuberculosis cases is presented and its impact analysed.
