TI  - T-cell co-stimulatory molecules: novel targets for the treatment of allergic 
      airway disease.
PG  - 383-90
AB  - The first two articles in this series discussed the fundamental concept of T-cell 
      co-stimulation as a key event in the induction of any immune response, in 
      addition to reviewing the current data on the role of co-stimulatory molecules 
      for the induction and progression of allergic airway diseases. Based on these 
      considerations, this final edition will delineate and discuss novel strategies 
      for the prevention and/or therapy of allergic diseases based upon the modulation 
      of co-stimulation.
