VI  - 25
IP  - 1
DP  - 2005 Jan
TI  - Pulmonary fibrosis in an individual occupationally exposed to inhaled indium-tin 
      oxide.
PG  - 200-4
AB  - Despite the increasing industrial use of indium-tin oxide (ITO) to manufacture 
      flat-panel displays, such as liquid-crystal displays or plasma display panels for 
      televisions, little is known about the potential health hazard induced by 
      occupational exposure to indium compounds. The current study describes a case of 
      fibrotic lung disease that developed after a 4-yr exposure to ITO. The pathology 
      of the lung demonstrated pulmonary fibrosis with the presence of cholesterol 
      granulomas. In conclusion, more attention needs to be paid to the possible toxic 
      effects of indium compounds, and maximum healthcare measures should be taken to 
      protect industry workers from these toxicities.
