TI  - Polyethylene flock-associated interstitial lung disease in a Spanish female.
PG  - 1610-2
AB  - This case study presents a female aged 54 yrs with a 12 months history of 
      progressive pulmonary impairment after a 7-yr period of occupational exposure to 
      rotary-cut polyethylene. An open lung biopsy revealed the histopathology of 
      follicular bronchiolitis that is viewed as a stereotypical feature for flock 
      worker's lung. It seems to be the first case of plastic flock-associated 
      interstitial lung disease reported outside North America.
