TI  - Patent foramen ovale causing position-dependent shunting in a patient, when 
      laying down her corset.
PG  - 731-3
AB  - A 75-yr-old female presented with platypnoea and orthodeoxia, shortly after 
      laying down an old and pinching corset. The injection of activated Haemaccel in 
      the right cubital vene during transoesophageal echocardiography, in the upright 
      position, revealed a direct blood flow from the superior caval vein at a patent 
      foremen ovale, consequently opening it and causing a large right-to-left shunt 
      which was calculated at 28.5%. In the supine position there was only a minimal 
      opening of the patent foremen ovale with a calculated right-to-left shunt of 
      9.5%. The patent foremen ovale was successfully closed percutaneously with a 
      CardioSEAL.
