TI  - Pulmonary veno-occlusive disease in myeloproliferative disorder.
PG  - 213-6
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00157707 [doi]
AB  - The present study reports a case of biopsy-proven pulmonary veno-occlusive 
      disease as a cause of severe pulmonary hypertension in a patient suffering from a 
      chronic myeloproliferative disorder. The pulmonary disease evolved favourably 
      under treatment with defibrotide, a pro-fibrinolytic medication used in hepatic 
      veno-occlusive disease.
