TI  - Tobacco use in relation to COPD and asthma.
PG  - 438-45
AB  - Smoking is the leading cause of preventable death worldwide. Hundreds of millions 
      of individuals still smoke, affecting their health as well as that of their 
      peers, family and offspring. Smoking is a well-established prime risk factor for 
      chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and hampers the response to treatment in 
      asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. In the present paper, new 
      concepts are discussed with respect to pathology, treatment, smoking cessation 
      and tobacco control. Recommendations for future directions are given.
