OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20130204
LR  - 20130523
IS  - 1399-3003 (Electronic)
IS  - 0903-1936 (Linking)
VI  - 40
IP  - 3
DP  - 2012 Sep
TI  - A 3-year longitudinal study of sleep disordered breathing in the elderly.
PG  - 665-72
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00133011 [doi]
AB  - Limited and controversial data exist on the natural evolution of sleep disordered 
      breathing (SDB) in untreated individuals. This study examines the evolution of 
      SDB over a 3-yr period in a community-based sample of elderly subjects. From the 
      initial cohort of 854 healthy subjects aged mean ± SD 68.4 ± 0.8 yrs, 519 
      untreated subjects accepted clinical and instrumental follow-up 3.6 ± 1.6 yrs 
      later. SDB was defined as a respiratory disturbance index (RDI) >15 events · 
      h(-1). At baseline, 202 (39%) subjects had an RDI ≤ 15 events · h(-1) and 317 
      (61%) had an RDI >15 events · h(-1). 3 yrs later, 280 (54%) subjects were non-SDB 
      and 239 (46%) had SDB. Between evaluations, the RDI decreased from 22.3 ± 16.2 to 
      16.4 ± 13.0 events · h(-1), with a greater decrease in the number of cases with 
      an RDI >30 events · h(-1) that in those with RDI ≥ 30 events · h(-1). In the 
      non-SDB group, 81% had a stable RDI and 19% increased their RDI by a mean of 13.7 
      events · h(-1). In the SDB group, the RDI decreased to values ≤ 15 events · h(-1) 
      in 36.6% of cases, 63.4% still having SDB. The RDI changes did not depend on 
      weight changes. In healthy elderly subjects, the prevalence and severity of SDB 
      did not show a tendency toward natural worsening, some cases having improvement 
      or a remission independent of weight changes. These findings also suggest that in 
      the elderly, natural SDB progression is still hypothetical.
