VI  - 38
IP  - 2
DP  - 2011 Aug
TI  - The best on infections: update from the 2010 ERS Congress.
PG  - 450-5
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00040011 [doi]
AB  - Respiratory tract infections and tuberculosis are among the leading reasons for 
      seeking medical care. In this report the most recent advances in the field of 
      clinical research and basic sciences of respiratory infections and tuberculosis 
      are presented through the analysis of some of the best abstracts presented at the 
      20th European Respiratory Society Congress in Barcelona, Spain and their 
      subsequent publications in major journals. The role of viruses in chronic 
      obstructive pulmonary disease exacerbations, the importance of new biomarkers in 
      the management and risk assessment of lower respiratory tract infections, new 
      modalities of treatment of respiratory infections as well as new tools for the 
      diagnosis of latent and active tuberculosis in special subgroups of patients 
      (children and immunocompromised individuals), and the new epidemiological threat 
      of multidrug-resistant and extensively drug-resistant tuberculosis cases are 
      discussed.
