TI  - Lives on the line? Ethics and practicalities of duty of care in pandemics and 
      disasters.
PG  - 303-9
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00041609 [doi]
AB  - Pandemics and acute emergencies raise pressing medical, ethical and 
      organisational challenges. These include global governance, priority setting, 
      triaging of patients, allocation of scarce resources and restricting individual 
      liberty in the interests of public health. We will focus particularly on an issue 
      of direct relevance to all respiratory team members, i.e. what is the duty of the 
      healthcare worker to continue working in the face of personal risk, and draw 
      lessons from guidelines, ethical considerations, past pandemics and evolving 
      experience with H1N1 swine influenza.
