DP  - 2008 Jul
TI  - Possible role of imatinib in clinical pulmonary veno-occlusive disease.
PG  - 232-5
LID - 10.1183/09031936.00054407 [doi]
AB  - The platelet-derived growth factor receptor inhibitor imatinib has demonstrated 
      clinical and haemodynamical improvement in both animal models of pulmonary 
      hypertension (PH) and patients with PH. It has been suggested that 
      anti-proliferative effects on pulmonary vascular smooth muscle cells are 
      responsible for these beneficial effects. The current study describes a patient 
      with pulmonary arterial hypertension associated with a suspected pulmonary 
      veno-occlusive disease. Treatment with imatinib resulted in rapid clinical 
      improvement and decrease of ground-glass opacities and lobular septal thickening 
      on high-resolution computed tomography. Based on these findings and on in vitro 
      effects of imatinib on permeability of the endothelium, the authors hypothesise 
      that the rapid clinical outcome is partly due to effects of imatinib on vascular 
      integrity.
