TI  - Lysosomal cysteine proteases in the lung: role in protein processing and 
      immunoregulation.
PG  - 620-8
AB  - Lysosomal cysteine proteases are a family comprising > 10 enzymes. For many years 
      it was believed that these enzymes catalyse protein breakdown unselectively, are 
      highly redundant in their substrate specificity and are also expressed 
      ubiquitously. This view has changed dramatically since a number of new lysosomal 
      cysteine proteases with restricted expression and outstanding enzymatic activity 
      have been described. In addition, knockout mice and selective protease inhibitors 
      have been used to characterise specific functions of single proteases. In this 
      review, some of these functions are discussed in relation to the lungs, 
      especially the role of lysosomal cysteine proteases in matrix remodelling, 
      immunoregulation and surfactant protein processing.
