VI  - 21
IP  - 5
DP  - 2003 May
TI  - Varicella pneumonia in adults.
PG  - 886-91
AB  - Varicella is a common contagious infection in childhood with increasing incidence 
      in adults. Pneumonia, although rare, is the most serious complication that 
      commonly affects adults. Over the last two decades there have been major advances 
      in the understanding of Varicella infections, management and prevention. This 
      review discusses the epidemiology, pathogenesis, pulmonary manifestation, 
      morbidity, long-term clinical consequences and current state of management of 
      Varicella pneumonia in adults. Prevention and other disease-modifying therapy are 
      also discussed.
